# Spellings that are not words of Romanian, folded into their accented sibling by
# tools/fold_diacritic_noise.py --nonwords whatever the reference wordlist says.
#
# Needed because no reference can decide this for Romanian. The LibreOffice ro_RO dictionary
# carries both spellings of a pair on purpose -- 92,092 of its 181,358 stems have diacritics,
# the rest are diacritic-free variants -- so it accepts "asa" exactly as it accepts "asa"'s
# accented form.
#
# Frequency cannot decide it either. A feminine noun takes its definite article by turning "ă"
# into "a", so "studentă"/"studenta", "gravidă"/"gravida" and "piatră"/"piatra" are regular
# grammatical pairs that differ by one diacritic and nothing else. Any rule that folds the plain
# spelling away deletes half the language's noun inflection.
#
# So this file is named, per word, and stays short. Add a spelling only when it is not a word of
# Romanian in any form -- not merely rarer than its accented sibling.
asa
